AB  - Machine learning modelling for time-series dynamics of the soil‒plant‒atmosphere continuum (SPAC) system is hindered by data sparsity and error accumulation in long-term predictions. This study addresses these two issues by developing a novel integrative data-driven framework, LocalGPgroup-Kalman, to maximize data utilization. Building upon the local Gaussian process (GP) group, it features: 1) data augmentation based on Markov chain Monte Carlo, recovering sufficient mechanistic information from limited field data and accounting for uncertainty; 2) a non-deterministic training strategy, incorporating uncertainty from the augmented datasets into the machine learning processes; and 3) a data assimilation approach with Kalman filter integrated into the machine learning model, leveraging uncertainty to improve predictions. Evaluated on real-world SPAC modelling tasks, the proposed framework demonstrated its capability to produce accurate SPAC system time-series predictions and to generalize across diverse scenarios. The study is expected to provide insights into comprehensive combination of data and mechanisms for SPAC system simulation.
